# Component Architecture

## Directory Structure

```
components/
├── common/          # Shared: dialogs/, TableGrid/, Button.tsx
├── inputs/          # Form inputs: InputField, DropDownSelector, CreatableTagSelector
├── layout/          # Layout: Page, Header, Footer
└── pages/           # Feature-oriented organization
    └── CourseContent/
        ├── Registration/   # Feature folder
        │   ├── index.tsx
        │   ├── types.ts
        │   └── hooks/
        └── AchievementRecord/
```

## Organization Principles

**✅ Feature-based** (preferred):
```
Registration/
├── index.tsx
├── RegistrationButton.tsx
├── RegistrationModal.tsx
└── hooks/useRegistrationHandler.ts
```

**❌ Technology-based** (avoid):
```
buttons/, modals/, forms/, hooks/
```

## Component Patterns

```typescript
// Container: Handles data and logic
const CourseContent: FC<{ id: number }> = ({ id }) => {
  const { data, loading, error } = useAdminQuery(QUERY, { variables: { id } });
  if (loading) return <CircularProgress />;
  if (error) return <ErrorMessageDialog error={error} />;
  return <CourseHeader course={data.course} />;
};

// Presentational: Pure UI
const CourseHeader: FC<{ course: Course }> = ({ course }) => (
  <h1>{course.title}</h1>
);
```

## Key Rules

- ✅ Organize by feature, not technology
- ✅ Extract complex logic to custom hooks
- ✅ Use composition over inheritance
- ✅ Check existing components before creating new ones
- ✅ Keep components under 200 lines
- ❌ Avoid deep nesting (max 3-4 levels)
- ❌ Avoid props drilling (use context/hooks)
